  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="9010e2e0-ea9f-5e1a-b795-88704761a9e7" activityNameId="eb67263a-12ed-5826-a3c8-581479c29f0a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Soybean oil, at oil mill</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Soybean oil, at oil mill
Inventory refers to the production of 1 kg soybean oil, respectively soybean meal (incl. hulls). The multioutput-process 'soybeans, in oil mill' delivers the co-products 'soybean oil, at oil mill' and 'soybean meal, at oil mill'. Economic allocation with allocation factor of 40.7% to oil and 59.3 to meal. Allocation is done according to carbon balance for CO2 emissions.;
UUID: 75a66aa0-62e5-303c-9023-376166ee4a12
This process includes the transport of soybeans to the mill, and the processing of soybeans to soybean oil and meal. System boundary is at the oil mill.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Typical oil mill designed for soybean oil solvent extraction (incl. pre-cracking of soybeans, dehulling, oil extraction, meal processing and oil purification), US context.
Time period: Data from 1998 to 2005, current technology for soybean oil extraction
Production volume: Approx. 50 Mt of soybeans were processed to oil and meal in 2005 in BR
Sampling: Data from US study, cross-checking with various literature sources, industrial data. Sources of energy supply from national statistics. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_75a66aa0-62e5-303c-9023-376166ee4a12.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
